ect", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "56677"} "1912"] "\n" [:option {:value "57175"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "57447"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "57741"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "58016"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "58263"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "58615"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "58981"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "59360"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "59753"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "60629"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "61146"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "61724"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "62288"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "62772"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "63414"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "64093"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "64779"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "65448"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "66133"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "257265"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "302537"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "358672"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000470"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2013628"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/57"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "4 × 100 metres Relay, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "20 – 21 October 1964"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/446"} "Kokuritsu Kyogijo, Shinjuku, Tokyo"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/60192"} "85 from 21 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The USA was probably the favorite but their team did not have the dominating runners of most years. But they were led by " [:a {:href "/athletes/78533"} "Bob Hayes"] ", who had won the 100 and was easily the top sprinter in the world. They were expected to be challenged by the French, led by " [:a {:href "/athletes/68452"} "Claude Piquemal"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/68179"} "Jocelyn Delecour"] ", and the Germans, but they failed to survive the semi-finals. With injuries to 100 metre runners " [:a {:href "/athletes/78592"} "Trent Jackson"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/78887"} "Mel Pender"] ", the US substituted 200 metre silver medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/78337"} "Paul Drayton"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/79091"} "Dick Stebbins"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "After some poor passing, the final exchange went to Hayes for the anchor, but by then he was his in fifth place, and at least three metres behind Delacour and Poland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/74707"} "Marian Dudziak"] ". And then Bob Hayes ran the fastest relay leg ever seen, possibly even still. Estimates of his 100 metre split are as low as 8.5-8.6 seconds, although most track statisticians think 8.80-8.90 is more likely. That would still be in the range of another stunning anchor run by " [:a {:href "/athletes/78692"} "Carl Lewis"] " at the Barcelona Olympics, 28 years later, and on an artificial surface track. Hayes won pulling away by almost three metres, having made up at least six metres on the other anchor runners. The rumor persists that Delecour told Mel Pender after the race, “All you guys had was Hayes”, and he responded, “He’s all we need, baby!”"] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "39.8 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "39.5 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "39.0 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td